{"uid":"accead64912773b2","name":"test_a_genuinely_fresh_os_process_re_entry_after_a_commit_still_sees_the_approach_as_progressed","fullName":"tests.test_approach_start_head_persistence#test_a_genuinely_fresh_os_process_re_entry_after_a_commit_still_sees_the_approach_as_progressed","historyId":"3012399a5a380aa70d578382ee8bb376","time":{"start":1791958292421,"stop":1791958293220,"duration":799},"description":"cure-01-01, requirement A.2's clause driven across a REAL process\n    boundary: commit -> episode ends mid-approach -> fresh-OS-process\n    re-entry -> stagnation, still on approach 1. The stalled approach is\n    archived and replanned (v0.36 requirement F.1) and the stagnation event\n    records `approachProgressed: True`.\n\n    Episode 1 (`_fresh_process_stagnation_episode.episode_one`, its own\n    `python -m` child process) creates the run-state tree and commits once;\n    its one-iteration budget ends the episode mid-approach.\n\n    Episode 2, a SECOND, independently spawned `python -m` child process --\n    no shared python object, module cache or event loop with episode 1's\n    process, or with this test's own -- re-enters `worker` over the\n    identical run root/workspace and runs a genuinely quiet round.\n    Pre-task-001 (`_step_worker` re-deriving `approach_start_head` fresh\n    from `self._workspace_head_sha()` at its own method entry instead of\n    reading `self._approach_start_head(approach)` back off `status.json`)\n    episode 2 fails inside its OWN process: the commit witness reads as\n    \"unchanged\", so the event says `approachProgressed: False`, episode 2's\n    own assertion raises and its process exits non-zero.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>cure-01-01, requirement A.2's clause driven across a REAL process<br />\nboundary: commit -&gt; episode ends mid-approach -&gt; fresh-OS-process<br />\nre-entry -&gt; stagnation, still on approach 1. The stalled approach is<br />\narchived and replanned (v0.36 requirement F.1) and the stagnation event<br />\nrecords <code>approachProgressed: True</code>.</p>\n<pre><code>Episode 1 (`_fresh_process_stagnation_episode.episode_one`, its own\n`python -m` child process) creates the run-state tree and commits once;\nits one-iteration budget ends the episode mid-approach.\n\nEpisode 2, a SECOND, independently spawned `python -m` child process --\nno shared python object, module cache or event loop with episode 1's\nprocess, or with this test's own -- re-enters `worker` over the\nidentical run root/workspace and runs a genuinely quiet round.\nPre-task-001 (`_step_worker` re-deriving `approach_start_head` fresh\nfrom `self._workspace_head_sha()` at its own method entry instead of\nreading `self._approach_start_head(approach)` back off `status.json`)\nepisode 2 fails inside its OWN process: the commit witness reads as\n&quot;unchanged&quot;, so the event says `approachProgressed: False`, episode 2's\nown assertion raises and its process exits non-zero.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791957838589,"stop":1791957838589,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791957838589,"stop":1791957838589,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791958292403,"stop":1791958292409,"duration":6},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791958292403,"stop":17919